# CQ-25 · annotation-below-threshold
#
# Question: Which annotated triples does the producer report below 0.80
#           confidence?
# Persona:  P1 — generation-pipeline engineer. The query a pipeline runs to
#           route low-confidence edges to review instead of to the renderer —
#           a gate the schema cannot express, because the schema has no opinion
#           about how confident is confident enough.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.11 (`vso:confidence`, bounded to [0,1] since v1.3)
# Form:     SELECT — one row per triple below the threshold
# Note:     0.80 is this query's threshold and nothing else's: VSON fixes no
#           confidence policy, and `vss:ConfidenceRangeShape` bounds the value
#           to [0,1] without preferring any part of the interval. The comparison
#           is numeric, so the `xsd:decimal` the transpiler emits and an
#           `xsd:double` from another producer are both ordered correctly.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?subject ?predicate ?object ?confidence
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?annotation a vso:Annotation ;
                vso:annotatedSubject   ?subject ;
                vso:annotatedPredicate ?predicate ;
                vso:annotatedObject    ?object ;
                vso:confidence         ?confidence .
    FILTER(?confidence < 0.80)
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?subject ?predicate
